<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="csp">
            <group id="general" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="0" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General</label>
                <field id="enabled_rules" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable whitelist</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Adds the entries of System > Content Security Policy > Whitelist to the policy, together with the csp_whitelist.xml files of installed modules.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enabled_reports" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Collect violation reports</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Browsers send violations to this store, where they can be reviewed and turned into whitelist entries. While this is on, it replaces the Report URI set in the Mode groups below.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_restrict_mode_adminhtml" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enforce the policy in the admin</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Browsers block everything the admin policy does not allow. Whitelist every service the admin loads, such as reCAPTCHA, before you enable this, or you may not be able to sign in.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_restrict_mode_frontend" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enforce the policy on the storefront</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Browsers block everything the storefront policy does not allow.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="add_all_storefront_urls" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Allow the hosts of every store view</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Adds the link, static and media hosts of all store views to the policy, for pages that load resources from another store view.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_header_splitting" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Split large policy headers</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Sends a policy larger than the limit below as several headers that together allow exactly what the single header allows. Related directives stay together and report-uri is repeated in every header. When that is not possible the header is sent whole, and a message appears in the admin.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="max_header_size" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Header size limit (bytes)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Largest value of one header. The headers of a split policy together are larger than the single header. Check the limits of your web server and proxies.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_header_splitting">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_value_optimization" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Optimize policy headers</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Removes duplicate sources. The steps below make the header smaller without changing what it allows, except for subdomain consolidation.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_redundant_wildcard_removal" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="90" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Remove hosts covered by a wildcard</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Removes a host such as www.example.com when *.example.com in the same directive allows every URL it allows.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_scheme_path_stripping" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="100" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Remove https:// from hosts on secure pages</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>On an HTTPS page a host without a scheme allows HTTPS only, so the prefix can be dropped. Ports and paths are kept.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_default_src_consolidation" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="110" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Remove redundant directives</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Removes a fetch directive when the directive it falls back to allows exactly the same for every kind of request. default-src, base-uri, form-action and frame-ancestors are never removed.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="enable_subdomain_wildcard_consolidation" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="120" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Replace subdomains of trusted domains with a wildcard</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Widens the policy: when enough subdomains of a trusted domain are allowed, they are replaced with *.domain, which allows every subdomain of it.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="subdomain_wildcard_parents" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="130" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Trusted domains</label>
                    <backend_model>Hryvinskyi\Csp\Model\Config\Backend\TrustedParentDomains</backend_model>
                    <comment>One domain per line, such as example.com. Only subdomains of these domains are replaced with a wildcard.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                        <field id="enable_subdomain_wildcard_consolidation">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="subdomain_wildcard_threshold" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="140" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Subdomains needed for a wildcard</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-digits-range digits-range-2-1000</validate>
                    <comment>Least number of allowed subdomains of a trusted domain that are replaced with a wildcard.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enable_value_optimization">1</field>
                        <field id="enable_subdomain_wildcard_consolidation">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="debug_mode_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="9999" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Debug log</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Writes the module's diagnostics to var/log/hryvinskyi/csp.log.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="report_ingestion" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Violation Report Limits</label>
                <field id="rate_limit" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Violations per client per minute</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Further reports of a client are ignored until the next minute. Behind a proxy or CDN, configure Magento's remote address so that clients are told apart.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="max_body_bytes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Largest report (bytes)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Larger report requests are ignored without being read.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="report_cleanup" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Violation Report Cleanup</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Clean up automatically</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Deletes old violation reports every night, and the pending report groups left without reports.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Cleanup mode</label>
                    <source_model>Hryvinskyi\Csp\Model\Config\Source\CleanupMode</source_model>
                    <comment>By date deletes reports not seen for the threshold in days; by record count keeps the threshold number of most recently seen reports.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="threshold" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Threshold</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Days for the date mode, reports to keep for the record count mode.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
